maspsx: a nop after a load when the next instruction is an li into the loaded register

For the assembler versions before 2.30 only (the switch that already puts a
nop between two loads into one register, nop_lw_lw). The original assembler
of this game's library (version 2.21 in this project's configuration) has a
nop between `lhu $2,396($3)` and `li $2,0xffff` in _spu_init at 0x8016bb58,
the one place of the game where a load is followed by an li into the same
register; the compiler prints `#nop` there and leaves the choice to the
assembler. With this rule the function builds to the original's bytes, and
no other unit of the build changes.

This file is a change to maspsx (https://github.com/mkst/maspsx, MIT license,
Copyright (c) 2023 Mark Street), against the commit that `build.toml` pins.
The build applies it to its export of that commit; the checkout is not touched.

--- a/maspsx/__init__.py
+++ b/maspsx/__init__.py
@@ -112,6 +112,11 @@
         if re.match(rf"^{r_source},.*$", rest):
             return True
 
+    elif op == "li":
+        # ASPSX < 2.30 behaviour: li into the register that was just loaded
+        if loads_to_reg and re.match(rf"^{r_source},.*$", rest):
+            return True
+
     elif op == "lwc2":
         # lwc2 $5, 4( $4 )
         if re.match(rf"^.*\(\s*{r_source}\s*\)$", rest):
